// UpsertAimMcpProxyWithBodyWithResponse Create or update an MCP proxy from its spec
//
// Create or update a single-upstream MCP proxy, identified by the `hrid` carried in the body. Re-applying an
// unchanged spec is a no-op. A first apply creates the proxy and, unless `state` is `STOPPED`, starts it; a
// later apply converges the mutable parts — `name`, `description`, `proxy`, `contextPath`, the identity
// providers and the plan set — and, while the proxy runs, redeploys it once. The lifecycle converges too: `STARTED`
// starts a stopped proxy, `STOPPED` stops a running one and keeps later changes stored until the next
// `STARTED`. Policy flows are owned by the declaration: the proxy's flows and each declared plan's flows are
// replaced by the declared ones whenever they differ, and a flow the declaration no longer carries is
// removed. Identity providers converge by name: a declared provider the proxy does not have is attached
// as a resource of its API, a declared provider whose configuration differs from the proxy's resource is
// rejected — except a generic provider's `clientSecret`, which replaces the stored one when it differs and
// is kept when omitted — and a resource the declaration no longer names is left in place. The `GRAVITEE_AM`
// provider is provisioned when the proxy is created and cannot be added later. Plans converge by name: a declared plan
// the proxy does not have is created and published, a plan the proxy holds in staging is published, a plan
// the declaration no longer carries is closed — closing terminates its subscriptions — and a deprecated plan
// is rejected, as APIM cannot publish it again. `entityId` is fixed at creation, and a plan cannot be changed
// in place under the same name: declaring a different value is rejected rather than applied. The upstream
// server is not contacted — the gateway reaches it at runtime.
// A `STUDIO` (`mode: STUDIO`) is declared from servers registered under `catalog/mcp-servers`: `studio.tools`
// names each tool by its server's HRID and runtime name, converges as a set and replaces the studio's tool
// surface when it changes; `studio.upstreamAuth` converges per server; `studio.enableFGA` inserts or removes
// the platform's authorization flow. `mode` is fixed at creation.
// Findings that prevent the apply are reported in `errors.severe` with a `400`, and nothing is persisted or
// destroyed. A dry run performs the same checks. A start or a deploy the gateway side refuses answers `500`
// with the technical code `gamma.mcp.lifecycle.failed`: the declaration is stored and the next apply retries,
// redeploying a running proxy APIM reports out of sync even when nothing changed.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PUT /aim/mcp-proxies (the `UpsertAimMcpProxy` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) UpsertAimMcpProxyWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, params *UpsertAimMcpProxyParams, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*UpsertAimMcpProxyResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.UpsertAimMcpProxyWithBody(ctx, params, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseUpsertAimMcpProxyResponse(rsp)
}

